        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by incorrect handling of filesystem sizes and related values when they exceed 8 TB, leading to potential overflow or incorrect calculations in 32-bit representations. The original logic did not properly account for the need to shift values down when they exceeded the maximum representable size in a 32-bit integer, resulting in inaccurate values for size, available space, and used space.

